// Server stopped reporting to Defender
//
// Fires when a server that was sending process telemetry goes quiet for 4 hours. That's
// what an EDR killer looks like from the console.
//
// Runs:      Every 3 hours
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1562.001, T1562.006
// Tables:    DeviceProcessEvents
// Custom details: LastTelemetry
//
// Needs:
//   - Scope the rule to a server device group. Laptops go offline all the time and will
//     spam you.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check if the server is actually up, and if there's planned maintenance.
//   - Escalate right away if the server is up but silent.
//   - Close if it's a planned outage or it was decommissioned.
//
// Tune: SilentFor at the top of the query.

let SilentFor = 4h;
DeviceProcessEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(12h)
| summarize (Timestamp, ReportId) = arg_max(Timestamp, ReportId) by DeviceId, DeviceName
| where Timestamp < ago(SilentFor)
| extend LastTelemetry = Timestamp
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, LastTelemetry
